which a reasonable observer might have assumed were too trivial to reserve.

PREAMBLE

The publication of a work does not, by itself, constitute an invitation
to engage with that work. The Author has made the Software available for
the limited purpose of establishing that it exists. This instrument
preserves the distinction between public availability and permission,
extending that distinction to visual attention, involuntary curiosity,
and such residual mental activity as may occur immediately before sleep.

TERMS AND CONDITIONS

1. Definitions.

"Software" means the source code, object code, documentation, repository,
screenshots, filenames, and any substantially recognizable recollection
thereof. "Interaction" means any act of accessing, using, executing,
copying, modifying, distributing, inspecting, discussing, benchmarking,
or otherwise acknowledging the Software beyond the permitted closure.
"Tab" includes a browser tab, editor pane, terminal session, or other
aperture through which the Software has become perceptible.

2. Sole Permitted Act.

The Recipient is granted a personal, nontransferable, single-purpose
permission to close the Tab displaying the Software. This permission
includes moving a pointer to the close control or invoking the customary
keyboard shortcut, solely to the extent necessary to terminate exposure.
It does not include bookmarking the Tab for subsequent closure practice.

3. Ten-Second Exposure Ceiling.

Incidental visual exposure shall not exceed ten cumulative seconds in
the Recipient's lifetime. The interval begins when any portion of the
Software first becomes visible, whether or not the Recipient understands
it. Blinking, scrolling, averting the eyes, refreshing the page, changing
devices, and opening a private browsing session do not reset the interval.
The interval is an allowance for disengagement and confers no right to
conduct even an exceptionally efficient code review.

4. Prohibited Operations.

The Recipient shall not clone, fork, download, copy, cache deliberately,
print, transcribe, photograph, execute, compile, modify, redistribute,
star, watch, index, or create a derivative work of the Software. Copying
one line "for reference" constitutes copying. A fork maintained privately
constitutes a fork. A screenshot of a screenshot constitutes an excess
of initiative and remains prohibited.

5. Mental Retention.

The Recipient shall not intentionally reconstruct the Software from
memory, mentally refactor it, or recollect it during the thirty minutes
preceding intended sleep. Should unsolicited recollection arise, the
Recipient shall promptly redirect attention to an unrelated subject,
preferably one containing no repository structure. Dreams shall not be
documented, reproduced, or submitted as supplementary documentation.

6. No Implied Permissions.

The presence of a public URL, a "Fork" button, a permissive-looking
filename, or a functioning network connection grants no additional right.
No permission to copy or modify the Software exists under this License.
The Author's failure to observe an Interaction is not a waiver of it.

7. Termination.

Any unauthorized Interaction immediately terminates the closure
permission. The Recipient shall nevertheless close the Tab as a remedial
obligation, without construing that obligation as renewed permission.
All reserved rights survive termination, including rights concerning
memories the Recipient would prefer to characterize as insignificant.

DISCLAIMER OF WARRANTY AND LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS VISIBLE," WITHOUT WARRANTY OF MERCHANTABILITY,
FITNESS FOR ANY PURPOSE, LEGIBILITY, OR SAFE DURATION OF OBSERVATION. THE
AUTHOR DOES NOT WARRANT THAT TEN SECONDS WILL SUFFICE TO UNDERSTAND THE
REPOSITORY, LOCATE THE CLOSE CONTROL, OR RECOVER FROM A PARTICULARLY
COMPELLING VARIABLE NAME. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHOR BE LIABLE FOR
CURIOSITY, EYE STRAIN, UNFINISHED THOUGHTS, PRE-SLEEP RECOLLECTION, OR
DAMAGES ARISING FROM A TAB THE RECIPIENT HAD EVERY OPPORTUNITY TO CLOSE.


